BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[HEP Seminar] RG improved (optimized) perturbation: chiral symmetr
 y breaking and QCD thermodynamics — Jean-Loic Kneur (University of Montp
 ellier)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T140000
DTSTAMP:20261020T070000Z
UID:2880@physics.ucsd.edu
DESCRIPTION:<b>Speaker:</b> Jean-Loic Kneur (University of Montpellier)<br
 ><br><b>Abstract: </b>We discuss a specific Renormalization Group (RG) res
 ummation of perturbative expansions that can give nontrivial results for t
 he order parameters of chiral symmetry breaking in QCD. We illustrate in p
 articular the quark condensate obtained up to five-loop order using the Di
 rac spectral density and related Banks-Casher relation\, and compared to L
 attice QCD results. We then discuss extensions of this approach to hot QCD
 \, or to cold and dense QCD. For hot QCD a drastically reduced residual re
 normalization scale dependence is obtained as compared to standard perturb
 ative QCD. For cold and dense quark matter the three-loop RG-improved equa
 tion of state is used to obtain mass-radius relations for pure quark or hy
 brid hadron-quark compact stars\, which are compared to recent astrophysic
 al observations.<br><br><b>Speaker Biography: </b>Jean-Loic Kneur is curre
 ntly the CNRS Director of Research in the Charles Coulomb Lab in Montpelli
 er\, France. His main research topics have included: higher order correcti
 ons in Standard Model and supersymmetric models\, supersymmetry and neutra
 lino dark matter phenomenology\, composite (pseudo-Goldstone) Higgs models
 \, Effective Theories for thermal QCD (Hard Thermal Loop)\, and more recen
 tly\, applications to neutron stars.<br><br><a href="https://physics.ucsd.
 edu/events/seminars-colloquia">https://physics.ucsd.edu/events/seminars-co
 lloquia</a>
LOCATION:MYR-A 5623
END:VEVENT
