BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[HEP Seminar] A Witten effect for global monopoles — Pablo Quíl
 ez Lasanta
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261103T140000
DTSTAMP:20261016T070000Z
UID:2864@physics.ucsd.edu
DESCRIPTION:<b>Speaker:</b> Pablo Quílez Lasanta<br><br>Abstract:<br><br>
 Global monopoles can carry electric charge even when the scalar fields tha
 t form them are neutral. I will show how an interaction usually discarded 
 as a total derivative produces a Witten effect for these global defects\, 
 giving them an electric charge proportional to their winding number. I wil
 l explain its origin and illustrate the mechanism in a simple UV completio
 n.<br><br>Based on arXiv:2610.14168 [hep-ph]<br><br>Bio:<br>Pablo Quílez 
 Lasanta received his PhD from the Universidad Autónoma de Madrid and the 
 Instituto de Física Teórica (IFT)\, followed by postdoctoral positions a
 t DESY (Hamburg) and UC San Diego. He is currently a Marie Skłodowska-Cur
 ie Fellow at CERN\, and will join the University of Barcelona next year on
  a tenure-track position. His research focuses on axions and axion-like pa
 rticles\, effective field theories and Hilbert series\, and more recently 
 on formal aspects of partial-wave unitarity and topological defects.<br><b
 r><a href="https://physics.ucsd.edu/events/seminars-colloquia">https://phy
 sics.ucsd.edu/events/seminars-colloquia</a>
LOCATION:MYR-A 5623
END:VEVENT
